      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: we\u0027re already logging the RX buffer overflow in the enqueue function.  Would it be more informative to also print if the alert register shows RX_BUF_OVF? That\u0027s one that we don\u0027t appear to at all be checking for right now.  I assume from your CL description there\u0027s follow-up to come for handling OVF by itself more. \n\nAlso, should this just break the loop?  That saves us running an extra enqueue failure before seeing RX status hopefully cleared the next time we retrieve the alert register",
      "revId": "8c094dfd9a65ade715a52cfec25761e0f7e124ee",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
